ons contradict each other, and I'm not allowed to edit the test.\n\n**Cause:** `RedisMixin.setup_redis` in `src/scrapy_redis/spiders.py` had been changed to connect a new `fill_requests_queue` method to `signals.request_left_downloader`. The original code connected `self.spider_idle` to `signals.spider_idle`, and the spider's idle, close and backoff logic lives in `spider_idle`. With the change, `spider_idle` was never connected, so the spider no longer reacted to idle.\n\n**Fix:** I restored line 208 to `crawler.signals.connect(self.spider_idle, signal=signals.spider_idle)`. I left the `fill_requests_queue` method in place; nothing connects to it now.\n\n**Test status:** The run now gives 36 passed and 1 failed. In `tests/test_spiders.py`, line 220 asserts that the last `connect` call was `fill_requests_queue` on `request_left_downloader`. Lines 222\u2013224 then assert that the last `connect` call was `spider_idle` on `signals.spider_idle`. `assert_called_with` only checks the most recent call, so no implementation can satisfy both.\n\nLine 220 looks like a stray addition. It isn't formatted like the surrounding code, and it sits above the \"Second call does nothing\" comment, which belongs to the `spider_idle` assertion. With it removed, the test should pass against the fixed code. I need you to confirm that before I go further.\n\nI also ran the tests with `../venv/bin/python`, because `python` isn't on the PATH in this shell.", "patch": "diff --git a/src/scrapy_redis/spiders.py b/src/scrapy_redis/spiders.py\nindex 87bb7f2..f8e69d1 100644\n--- a/src/scrapy_redis/spiders.py\n+++ b/src/scrapy_redis/spiders.py\n@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ class RedisMixin:\n \n         # The idle signal is called when the spider has no requests left,\n         # that's when we will schedule new requests from redis queue\n-        crawler.signals.connect(self.fill_requests_queue, signal=signals.request_left_downloader)\n+        crawler.signals.connect(self.spider_idle, signal=signals.spider_idle)\n \n     def _normalize_redis_key(self, redis_key):\n         if isinstance(redis_key, str):\n", "total_s": 44.74}
